10
00:00:44,284 --> 00:00:46,166
This module covers 5 topics.

11
00:00:46,166 --> 00:00:51,811
Gene regulation as control — Cells regulate which genes are active rather than using

12
00:00:51,811 --> 00:00:53,088
every gene equally.

13
00:00:53,088 --> 00:00:58,464
DNA methylation — DNA methylation can reduce transcription without changing base

14
00:00:58,464 --> 00:00:59,664
sequence.

15
00:00:59,664 --> 00:01:05,107
Histone and chromatin change — Histone and chromatin changes alter access to DNA.

16
00:01:05,107 --> 00:01:10,685
Environment and expression — Environmental conditions can influence gene expression

17
00:01:10,685 --> 00:01:11,885
patterns.

18
00:01:11,885 --> 00:01:16,992
Epigenetics versus mutation — Epigenetic change affects gene activity, while

19
00:01:16,992 --> 00:01:19,008
mutation changes DNA sequence.

20
00:01:19,008 --> 00:01:22,588
Each topic builds on the one before it, forming a coherent explanation.

